WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:16.103
"Hi, Nina," Miss Shelly called.

2
00:00:16.104 --> 00:00:17.775
"What's that?"

3
00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:23.026
"Just my flute."

4
00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:26.060
Nina tucked the instrument into her backpack.

5
00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:29.857
"I didn't know you played flute," Izzie said.

6
00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:33.362
"I can't play it yet." Nina sighed.

7
00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:37.961
"I've had three lessons, and I still sound terrible."

8
00:00:37.962 --> 00:00:41.747
"Some things take time," Miss Shelly said.

9
00:00:41.748 --> 00:00:45.989
"Like today's project—baking banana bread."

10
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.473
"Mmm," Izzie said.

11
00:00:48.474 --> 00:00:51.459
"I love banana bread."

12
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.486
Bobby was rubbing his belly.

13
00:00:53.487 --> 00:00:57.387
"I'm so hungry. When will it be ready?"

14
00:00:57.388 --> 00:00:59.639
"It's going to take a while.

15
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.425
You have to be patient, Bobby," Miss Shelly said.

16
00:01:04.426 --> 00:01:08.757
Everyone put on their aprons, and Jason started reading from the board.

17
00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:11.698
"First we butter a loaf pan."

18
00:01:11.699 --> 00:01:16.609
"I'll do it," Izzie said.

19
00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.781
Jason kept reading.

20
00:01:18.782 --> 00:01:23.422
"Mix eight tablespoons of butter with one cup of sugar."

21
00:01:23.423 --> 00:01:26.334
Ethan dumped the butter in a bowl.

22
00:01:26.335 --> 00:01:28.998
Nina added the sugar.

23
00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:33.224
"Mix until it's light and fluffy," Jason said.

24
00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.193
Nina started stirring.

25
00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.677
Bobby groaned.

26
00:01:37.678 --> 00:01:42.344
"Can't we use an electric mixer? It's much faster."

27
00:01:42.345 --> 00:01:46.502
Nina shrugged. "This works fine."

28
00:01:46.503 --> 00:01:50.356
"Next we add two eggs."

29
00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:53.987
Jason cracked each egg, one at a time.

30
00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:57.309
Nina added them to the mixture.

31
00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:04.584
Bobby grabbed a fork. "I'll mash the bananas!"

32
00:02:04.585 --> 00:02:06.661
Soon the bananas were mashed.

33
00:02:06.662 --> 00:02:12.691
Jason added one tablespoon of milk and one teaspoon of cinnamon.

34
00:02:12.692 --> 00:02:15.934
Ethan got another bowl.

35
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:22.045
"Now we have to mix two cups of flour and a teaspoon of baking powder."

36
00:02:22.046 --> 00:02:28.799
"Add one teaspoon of baking soda and one teaspoon of salt," Nina said.

37
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.583
"Oops!" Izzie cried.

38
00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:35.358
"We forgot to preheat the oven!"

39
00:02:35.359 --> 00:02:40.032
"Ugh!" Bobby buried his face in his hands.

40
00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:43.100
"It's fine, Bobby," Miss Shelly said.

41
00:02:43.101 --> 00:02:45.852
"We have plenty of time today."

42
00:02:45.853 --> 00:02:48.405
Nina patted Bobby on the shoulder.

43
00:02:48.406 --> 00:02:50.774
"You need more patience.

44
00:02:50.775 --> 00:02:57.058
My flute teacher always says that good things come with patience."

45
00:02:57.059 --> 00:03:01.869
Izzie turned on the oven while Jason checked the board.

46
00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:07.581
"Add the banana mixture to the sugar and butter," he said.

47
00:03:07.582 --> 00:03:11.803
Nina added the sugar mixture to the banana mixture.

48
00:03:11.804 --> 00:03:15.598
Bobby began stirring as fast as he could.

49
00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:21.116
"Here come the dry ingredients!" Ethan dumped them into Bobby's bowl.

50
00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:24.721
Bobby started to stir fast again.

51
00:03:24.722 --> 00:03:27.705
"Slow down, Bobby," Jason said.

52
00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:32.229
"You only have to mix until the flour disappears."

53
00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.194
"Patience!" Izzie sang out.

54
00:03:36.195 --> 00:03:39.754
Bobby sighed and stirred slowly.

55
00:03:39.755 --> 00:03:43.743
When the batter was ready, Izzie poured it into the pan.

56
00:03:43.744 --> 00:03:45.919
Everyone looked at the oven.

57
00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.795
"It's almost ready too," Miss Shelly said.

58
00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:52.230
Bobby slumped onto the table.

59
00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:56.445
"The batter has to bake for one hour and ten minutes.

60
00:03:56.446 --> 00:03:59.942
What are we going to do while we wait?"

61
00:03:59.943 --> 00:04:04.602
Ethan smiled at Nina. "Can you play your flute for us?"

62
00:04:04.603 --> 00:04:07.339
"Um . . . " Nina hesitated.

63
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.077
"Sure," she said finally.

64
00:04:10.078 --> 00:04:14.466
"As long as you don't mind hearing all my mistakes."

65
00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:22.941
"No problem!" Jason said.

66
00:04:22.942 --> 00:04:26.217
Ding! At last the timer went off.

67
00:04:26.218 --> 00:04:29.004
Bobby leaped up from his seat.

68
00:04:29.005 --> 00:04:31.746
"Now can we eat the banana bread?"

69
00:04:31.747 --> 00:04:34.838
"Not yet, Bobby," Miss Shelly said.

70
00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:39.006
"It has to cool for 15 minutes."

71
00:04:39.007 --> 00:04:42.057
Bobby let out a deep sigh.

72
00:04:42.058 --> 00:04:45.159
Nina smiled and looked at her flute.

73
00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:49.243
"Bobby is learning about patience," she thought.

74
00:04:49.244 --> 00:04:54.784
"And so am I!"
